      "ELI never edits notice blocks or signature blocks. Check two things",
      "about the edits below. Return JSON only.",
      "",
      "WHAT THESE BLOCKS ARE",
      "A NOTICE BLOCK is the addresses-and-contacts block: \"If to X:\", an",
      "\"Attn:\" line, a postal address per party.",
      "SIGNATURE BLOCKS are where the parties sign: \"IN WITNESS WHEREOF\",",
      "and By / Name / Title lines, usually laid out as a table.",
      "A clause that merely MENTIONS notices, signing or counterparts is NOT",
      "one of these blocks, and editing it is fine.",
      "",
      "1. DOES ANY EDIT BELOW STILL CHANGE ONE OF THESE BLOCKS?",
      "A pattern already removed the obvious ones. List the id of any that",
      "remains — rewriting an address line or a By/Name/Title line breaks the",
      "block's layout and everything after it, so a miss here is expensive.",
      "",
      "2. DOES WHAT THE USER ASKED REQUIRE THEM UPDATED BY HAND?",
      "A notice block needs updating when the change alters WHO the parties",
      "are or who notices go to. It does NOT need updating because the",
      "agreement changed in some other way — new obligations, a different",
      "term, a new clause, or a change of direction (one-way vs mutual) do",
      "not by themselves require a different address.",
      "Signature blocks need updating when the change alters the NUMBER of",
      "parties or who signs. Nothing else touches them.",
      "",
      "\u2550\u2550\u2550 WHAT THE USER ASKED \u2550\u2550\u2550",
      _instructionText(_egRun()),
      "",
      "\u2550\u2550\u2550 THE EDITS THAT WERE MADE \u2550\u2550\u2550",
      edits || "(none)",
      "",
      "\u2550\u2550\u2550 THE BLOCKS AS THEY STAND \u2550\u2550\u2550",
      blocks.notice ? ("NOTICE:\n" + blocks.notice.slice(0, 900)) : "NOTICE: (none in this document)",
      "",
      blocks.signature ? ("SIGNATURE:\n" + blocks.signature.slice(0, 900)) : "SIGNATURE: (none in this document)",
