  // Two lists, not one. MUST is what the change left wrong — the document
  // is inconsistent or the request is not actually done, and someone has to
  // act. SUGGESTED is everything the agent noticed but nobody asked for.
  //
  // Only MUST is shown. Suggestions collapse, because the point of this
  // panel is to make the after-work small: a list that mixes "your notice
  // block is now wrong" with "you could add late-payment interest" makes
  // both look optional.
